    <div class="styleguide-origin-panel">
      <div class="styleguide-origin-media">
        <img src="{{ '/images/misc/Thai-Emblem_white.png' | url }}" alt="Garuda, the Thai royal emblem, as printed in a Thai passport" class="styleguide-origin-mark">
      </div>
      <div class="styleguide-origin-copy">
        <span class="styleguide-type-label">Origin & Symbolism</span>
        <h3>Garuda</h3>
        <p>The mark is the Garuda, or Phra Khrut Pha — the emblem printed in a Thai passport and used as the official seal of the Thai monarchy and government. In Hindu mythology, Garuda is a divine being, half man and half eagle, the king of birds and the vahana, or mount, of the god Vishnu. Thai tradition adopted Garuda as a symbol of the monarchy itself, framing the king as an earthly extension of Vishnu's protection.</p>
        <p>Garuda's mythology carries specific traits: speed, elevated vision, and standing as the natural enemy of the Naga, the serpent beings of the underworld — a recurring struggle between sky and ground, clarity and concealment. Carried into a personal mark, it reads as an origin marker rather than a borrowed royal symbol: a fixed point back to a Thai passport and a lineage, translated into a system built on precision, altitude, and signal over noise.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
