    <div class="styleguide-print-rules" aria-label="Print typography rules">
      <article class="styleguide-print-panel styleguide-print-panel--specimen">
        <span class="styleguide-type-label">Print Specimen / DIN 2014 + Barlow</span>
        <h3>Field Guide Notes</h3>
        <p>Printed pages should feel quiet, precise, and editorial. Use the brand colors as measured signals, not full-page decoration unless the spread is acting as a divider or cover.</p>
      </article>

      <article class="styleguide-print-panel">
        <span class="styleguide-type-label">Page Grid</span>
        <ul>
          <li>Use a 12-column grid for letter and tabloid layouts.</li>
          <li>Keep outer margins at 0.5in minimum; use 0.75in for text-heavy documents.</li>
          <li>Align captions, rules, and metadata to the same vertical column as the image or text block they describe.</li>
          <li>Leave one generous quiet edge on covers, dividers, and portfolio plates.</li>
        </ul>
      </article>

      <article class="styleguide-print-panel">
        <span class="styleguide-type-label">Print Type Scale</span>
        <ul>
          <li>Cover title: 54-96pt DIN 2014 Light, tight leading.</li>
          <li>Section title: 28-44pt DIN 2014 Light.</li>
          <li>Body copy: 9.5-11pt Barlow Light with 14-16pt leading.</li>
          <li>Captions and metadata: 6.5-8pt Space Mono, uppercase only when brief.</li>
        </ul>
      </article>

      <article class="styleguide-print-panel">
        <span class="styleguide-type-label">Composition</span>
        <ul>
          <li>Keep paragraphs between 45 and 70 characters per line.</li>
          <li>Avoid widows, orphans, and single-word last lines.</li>
          <li>Use optical alignment for large display type, especially at page edges.</li>
          <li>Use hairline rules at 0.25pt to 0.5pt; never below 0.25pt for production print.</li>
        </ul>
      </article>

      <article class="styleguide-print-panel">
        <span class="styleguide-type-label">Print Color</span>
        <ul>
          <li>Convert RGB brand values to CMYK with proofing before press output.</li>
          <li>Use rich black for full-bleed black fields; use 100K for small text.</li>
          <li>Keep small reversed text at 8pt or larger and avoid thin weights over busy imagery.</li>
          <li>Use magenta and cyan as spot-like accents: rules, folios, tags, and data marks.</li>
        </ul>
      </article>

      <article class="styleguide-print-panel">
        <span class="styleguide-type-label">Export</span>
        <ul>
          <li>Export PDF/X-4 when transparency or image-heavy work is involved.</li>
          <li>Use 0.125in bleed for full-bleed pages and keep live text 0.25in from trim.</li>
          <li>Raster imagery should be 300ppi at final size; line art should stay vector.</li>
          <li>Embed or outline fonts only at final handoff, preserving editable source files separately.</li>
        </ul>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

