    <div class="styleguide-color-rules" aria-label="Color usage and print rules">
      <article class="styleguide-color-rule styleguide-color-rule--mix">
        <span class="styleguide-type-label">Usage Ratio</span>
        <div class="styleguide-color-ratio" aria-label="Recommended color usage ratio">
          <span style="--ratio: 45%; --ratio-color: #0e0f11;">45</span>
          <span style="--ratio: 25%; --ratio-color: #141518;">25</span>
          <span style="--ratio: 12%; --ratio-color: #c8289a;">12</span>
          <span style="--ratio: 8%; --ratio-color: #4fc8e8;">8</span>
          <span style="--ratio: 5%; --ratio-color: #7ac45a;">5</span>
          <span style="--ratio: 5%; --ratio-color: #e8a020;">5</span>
        </div>
        <p>Let black and graphite do the atmospheric work. Use magenta as the main signal, cyan for secondary readouts, and green or amber only when the content needs status meaning.</p>
      </article>

      <article class="styleguide-color-rule">
        <span class="styleguide-type-label">Screen Rules</span>
        <ul>
          <li>Use no more than two accent colors in a single UI section.</li>
          <li>Reserve magenta for active states, key links, selected filters, and focal data.</li>
          <li>Use cyan for supporting data, external links, and technical readouts.</li>
          <li>Do not set long body text in accent colors.</li>
        </ul>
      </article>

      <article class="styleguide-color-rule">
        <span class="styleguide-type-label">Print Rules</span>
        <ul>
          <li>Proof RGB-to-CMYK conversions before final output; expect cyan and magenta to dull on uncoated stock.</li>
          <li>Use 100K black for small text and rich black only for large fields, covers, and full-bleed panels.</li>
          <li>Keep reversed body copy at 8pt or larger, and avoid reversing thin Space Mono captions from saturated color.</li>
          <li>For brand-critical pieces, specify spot magenta or run a press proof instead of trusting screen color.</li>
        </ul>
      </article>
